# ignore until Vue2 to Vue3 upgrade
CVE-2025-15284

# brace-expansion vendored inside gaxios's own node_modules (Google OAuth
# client dependency used by td.server). No non-breaking fix is available:
# the only npm-provided fix bumps mocha (a dev dependency, unrelated to
# gaxios) to a new major version just because it shares the same lockfile
# resolution graph. Same exception documented in
# .github/workflows/.npm-audit-ignore.txt (as the equivalent GHSA IDs).
# Remove once gaxios ships a release with a patched brace-expansion.
CVE-2026-13149
CVE-2026-14257

# docs/ contains fake example credentials (BITBUCKET_CLIENT_ID/SECRET =
# 'deadbeef...') used purely as documentation placeholders in
# docs/configure/*.md and the generated Jekyll site (docs/configure/*.html,
# docs/assets/search.json). Trivy's secret scanner flags these as real
# Bitbucket client IDs. Scoped to docs/ only and to this specific rule so a
# real secret elsewhere in the image would still be caught.
bitbucket-client-id docs/*
